WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.301 line:92%
-Welcome back to "Late Night."

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.669 line:92%
We're here with John Oliver.

00:00:02.669 --> 00:00:03.803 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
John, I do enjoy

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:05.372 size:88% position:44% line:92%
you mentioned Edinburgh,

00:00:05.372 --> 00:00:07.140 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is part
of your early career,

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:09.242 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I did not know --
because I did know that.

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:10.610 line:92%
I did not know that you wrot

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:13.013 align:start size:94% position:6%
for a morning show
in Great Britain.

00:00:13.013 --> 00:00:15.382 size:81% position:41%
-I did. That was one
of my first paid jobs,

00:00:15.382 --> 00:00:16.416 align:start size:94% position:6%
was there was a show
in England --

00:00:16.416 --> 00:00:18.018
I don't know if it was on
when you were there --

00:00:18.018 --> 00:00:19.652 align:start size:94% position:6%
called "The Big Breakfast"
on Channel 4.

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:23.423 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was like a morning zoo
radio show on TV

00:00:23.423 --> 00:00:26.860 size:84% position:42%
that looks like kind of
"Pee-Wee's Playhouse."

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:31.031
And, yeah, so I would like get
a week contract, here and there,

00:00:31.031 --> 00:00:35.435 align:start size:94% position:6%
and would basically write puns
and guest questions.

00:00:35.435 --> 00:00:37.837 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was fun
because it was fun getting pai

00:00:37.837 --> 00:00:39.539 size:78% position:39%
to do something that,
if it wasn't comedy,

00:00:39.539 --> 00:00:41.141 align:start size:94% position:6%
it was at least
comedy-adjacent.

00:00:41.141 --> 00:00:44.344 align:start size:94% position:6%
But the longer I did it,
the more I wanted to kind of

00:00:44.344 --> 00:00:47.213
find ways to do something
that I thought was funny.

00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:50.650 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it all came to a head
with an interview

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:51.418 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
with Tatyana Ali.

00:00:51.418 --> 00:00:52.218 line:92%
Do you remember Tatyana Ali?

00:00:52.218 --> 00:00:53.319 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-She was on "The Fresh Prince.

00:00:53.319 --> 00:00:54.587 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, of course.
Of course you remember.

00:00:54.587 --> 00:00:56.723 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah.
You seem offended.

00:00:56.723 --> 00:00:58.858 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.858 --> 00:01:00.226 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Do I?
Sir, yes.

00:01:00.226 --> 00:01:01.895 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yes, I remember Tatyana
and you all know

00:01:01.895 --> 00:01:03.530 align:start size:94% position:6%
Tatyana Ali."
-I can't believe you know

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:04.397 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
who she is.

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:06.599 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Ouch!

00:01:06.599 --> 00:01:10.837 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, there was this idea
that, well,

00:01:10.837 --> 00:01:12.639 align:start size:94% position:6%
they'll do
some emergency questions

00:01:12.639 --> 00:01:15.141 align:start size:94% position:6%
and like break glass,
little prop,

00:01:15.141 --> 00:01:15.909 size:78% position:39% line:92%
everything seems fun.

00:01:15.909 --> 00:01:19.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they just said,
"Just write us 50 questions.

00:01:19.379 --> 00:01:20.647 line:92%
So we wrote 50 like generic,

00:01:20.647 --> 00:01:23.116 size:84% position:42%
"What's it like working
on 'The Fresh Prince'?"

00:01:23.116 --> 00:01:25.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, I wrote
one question in there

00:01:25.285 --> 00:01:27.220
about what was happening
in the world at the time.

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:30.190 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it came up, unfortunately,
and it was --

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:32.358 align:start size:94% position:6%
I believe the question
she was then asked,

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:35.495 align:start size:94% position:6%
at like 6:50
in the morning was,

00:01:35.495 --> 00:01:37.030 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Conditions on the ground
in Kosovo

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:39.232 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
seem to be deteriorating.

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:41.134 align:start size:94% position:6%
Air strikes don't seem
to have worked.

00:01:41.134 --> 00:01:43.002 align:start size:94% position:6%
Would you send in
ground troops?"

00:01:43.002 --> 00:01:45.138 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.138 --> 00:01:48.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
I remember watching it happen,
the start the question,

00:01:48.441 --> 00:01:49.576 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
thinking, "Uh-oh.

00:01:49.576 --> 00:01:50.477 line:92%
Maybe he'll bail out of it

00:01:50.477 --> 00:01:51.711 align:start size:94% position:6%
when he realizes
this is a problem."

00:01:51.711 --> 00:01:52.979 align:start size:94% position:6%
He kept reading it
and it got to the end.

00:01:52.979 --> 00:01:55.348 align:start size:94% position:6%
I remember thinking,
"Well, that was a fun job,

00:01:55.348 --> 00:01:59.986 size:78% position:39%
but it does feel like
neither side of this

00:01:59.986 --> 00:02:00.887 line:92%
are a great fit for the other.

00:02:00.887 --> 00:02:02.422 align:start size:94% position:6%
Let's just go
our separate ways."

00:02:02.422 --> 00:02:04.424 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Did they know,
amongst the writing staff,

00:02:04.424 --> 00:02:07.494 align:start size:94% position:6%
were they sure, right away
who had written that?

00:02:07.494 --> 00:02:09.262 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:09.262 --> 00:02:10.163 size:81% position:41% line:92%
I think I'd kind of --

00:02:10.163 --> 00:02:12.599
We'd written it the previous day
and I think I'd made a kind of

00:02:12.599 --> 00:02:15.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Ha ha, we'll get this in
and it'll never get picked,"

00:02:15.068 --> 00:02:17.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I think it was very muc
a sense of,

00:02:17.937 --> 00:02:20.874 size:78% position:39%
there's no collective
responsibility here.

00:02:20.874 --> 00:02:21.774 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"There's a sword.

00:02:21.774 --> 00:02:22.909 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Please fall on it."

00:02:22.909 --> 00:02:23.443 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.443 --> 00:02:25.912 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I do want to talk to you
about some sad news.

00:02:25.912 --> 00:02:29.215 align:start size:94% position:6%
We've obviously talked
about the royal family befor

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:31.951 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you have graced us
with your presence.

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:33.419 line:92%
Prince Philip passed away.

00:02:33.419 --> 00:02:35.555 line:92%
How are you feeling about that

00:02:35.555 --> 00:02:36.189 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, thanks.

00:02:36.189 --> 00:02:37.824 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thanks.
-I appreciate it, yeah.

00:02:37.824 --> 00:02:38.558 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.558 --> 00:02:41.728 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, it's difficult,
isn't it?
-Sure.

00:02:41.728 --> 00:02:43.496 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-When a 99-year-old...

00:02:43.496 --> 00:02:45.165 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.165 --> 00:02:48.234 align:start size:94% position:6%
...such a checkered
moral history leaves us,

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:51.237 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's hard to know exactly ho
to feel, or, indeed,

00:02:51.237 --> 00:02:53.339 size:78% position:39%
whether to articulate
how you actually do.

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:55.642
It's difficult, isn't it?
-Mm-hmm, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:55.642 --> 00:02:58.344 align:start size:94% position:6%
You pointed out last night
on your show,

00:02:58.344 --> 00:03:00.847 size:88% position:44%
you reminded people --
which I had forgotten --

00:03:00.847 --> 00:03:03.516 size:81% position:41%
that he and the queen
were cousins, in fact.

00:03:03.516 --> 00:03:05.585 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They were very close.
They were.

00:03:05.585 --> 00:03:07.554 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
And I don't think it was jus

00:03:07.554 --> 00:03:09.822 align:start size:94% position:6%
restricted to them.
I believe that

00:03:09.822 --> 00:03:12.091 size:84% position:42% line:92%
that family is familiar

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:13.526 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
with one another.

00:03:13.526 --> 00:03:16.262 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, that speaks
to their closeness.

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:18.665 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughs ]
Speaks. That's right.

00:03:18.665 --> 00:03:20.533 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
What they --

00:03:20.533 --> 00:03:22.769 align:start size:94% position:6%
In the way that they can't b
close emotionally,

00:03:22.769 --> 00:03:24.470 align:start size:94% position:6%
they certainly are close
biologically

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:27.140 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I think that's something
isn't it?

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:28.408 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
Something you want to see

00:03:28.408 --> 00:03:33.613
on a tea service, you know
or a commemorative plate.

00:03:33.613 --> 00:03:35.114 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, it's tough.

00:03:35.114 --> 00:03:36.249 size:78% position:39% line:92%
I will say, you know,

00:03:36.249 --> 00:03:37.784 align:start size:94% position:6%
with that general rule
that, you know,

00:03:37.784 --> 00:03:39.052 align:start size:94% position:6%
you should not speak ill
of the dead,

00:03:39.052 --> 00:03:41.754
it feels like people were really
trying to do that, until -

00:03:41.754 --> 00:03:45.592
What you also can't do is spea
overly complimentary of the dead

00:03:45.592 --> 00:03:47.427
and it feels like, at that
point, all bets are off.

00:03:47.427 --> 00:03:49.662 align:start size:94% position:6%
Then, the people who have been
biting their tongue go,

00:03:49.662 --> 00:03:51.364 line:92%
"Actually, [bleep] you. No

00:03:51.364 --> 00:03:53.533 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Here's what he was like.

00:03:53.533 --> 00:03:55.535 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:55.535 --> 00:03:58.371 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You want to do something
which is very nice

00:03:58.371 --> 00:04:01.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I really think speaks
to your generosity.

00:04:01.608 --> 00:04:03.243 line:92%
We have a guest on tomorrow...

00:04:03.243 --> 00:04:05.078 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-Patrick Radden Keefe.

00:04:05.078 --> 00:04:06.546 size:88% position:44% line:92%
He's a wonderful author.

00:04:06.546 --> 00:04:07.247 size:88% position:44% line:92%
He has a book coming out

00:04:07.247 --> 00:04:09.482 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Amazing.
tonight, midnight tonight.

00:04:09.482 --> 00:04:10.350 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Absolutely amazing.

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:14.053
So, yeah, his last book,
I think might have been the book

00:04:14.053 --> 00:04:16.356
I've enjoyed the most
over the last couple of years --

00:04:16.356 --> 00:04:18.358 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I agree.
-about Northern Island.

00:04:18.358 --> 00:04:19.626 line:92%
I think about it all the time.

00:04:19.626 --> 00:04:20.860 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this new one is
about the Sackler family

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:23.963
and I have not been more excited
about a book for a long time

00:04:23.963 --> 00:04:26.366 align:start size:94% position:6%
Remember when the last
Harry Potter book came out

00:04:26.366 --> 00:04:28.868 align:start size:94% position:6%
and there were all those shots
of kids lined up

00:04:28.868 --> 00:04:30.169 line:92%
outside of Barnes &amp; Noble?

00:04:30.169 --> 00:04:32.338 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
-That's how I feel about this.

00:04:32.338 --> 00:04:34.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
If bookstores were still
technically a thing

00:04:34.073 --> 00:04:37.310
and if there wasn't a pandemic
I would be outside a bookstore

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:38.144 size:75% position:38% line:92%
at midnight tonight,

00:04:38.144 --> 00:04:40.680 size:81% position:41%
dressed like a member
of the Sackler family.

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:43.549 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:43.549 --> 00:04:45.351 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hey, thank you. It's always
so great to see you.

00:04:45.351 --> 00:04:48.755 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know,
you've been on the show a lot.

00:04:48.755 --> 00:04:50.857 size:84% position:42%
This is the first time
you've been on the show

00:04:50.857 --> 00:04:53.493 align:start size:94% position:6%
that West Ham
is slightly higher in the tabl

00:04:53.493 --> 00:04:54.761 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah.
-than Liverpool.

00:04:54.761 --> 00:04:56.362 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You're doing great.
Congratulations.

00:04:56.362 --> 00:04:59.132 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I feel like it's not
going to last,

00:04:59.132 --> 00:05:00.667 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I'm certainly
enjoying the ride.

00:05:00.667 --> 00:05:03.236
-It won't, but that's the
important thing, isn't it?

00:05:03.236 --> 00:05:04.671 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like eating
a delicious meal

00:05:04.671 --> 00:05:06.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you can't really afford
You're going to get

00:05:06.339 --> 00:05:07.607 align:start size:94% position:6%
to the end of it.
You're never going to have

00:05:07.607 --> 00:05:09.876 align:start size:94% position:6%
that experience again,
but enjoy it.

00:05:09.876 --> 00:05:12.645 line:92%
-Well, I will take that advice

00:05:12.645 --> 00:05:14.414 line:92%
-I would love West Ham to go -

00:05:14.414 --> 00:05:16.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would love us to both be
in the top 4.

00:05:16.182 --> 00:05:17.450
That would be great.
-That would be a perfect outcome

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:19.385 align:start size:94% position:6%
to this season.
-And if Chelsea could drop out

00:05:19.385 --> 00:05:21.821 align:start size:94% position:6%
because that's a blood sport
that they're playing.

00:05:21.821 --> 00:05:23.122 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:23.122 --> 00:05:24.023 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you, John.
I really do hope,

00:05:24.023 --> 00:05:26.259 align:start size:94% position:6%
one of these days,
we see you in person again

00:05:26.259 --> 00:05:27.660 line:92%
-Yeah, that would be great

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:30.563 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Last Week Tonight"
airs Sunday nights on HBO

00:05:30.563 --> 00:05:32.198 align:start size:94% position:6%
and is available
to stream on HBO Max.

00:05:32.198 --> 00:05:34.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
Patrick Radden Keefe's boo
"Empire of Pain:

00:05:34.167 --> 00:05:37.403 align:start size:94% position:6%
The Secret History of the
Sackler Dynasty" is out now.

